Relevant columns and how they will be used

`posts_answers.id` : answer identifier – joins to `votes.post_id`  
`posts_answers.parent_id` : id of the *question* that the answer belongs to – joins to `posts_questions.id`  
`posts_answers.owner_user_id` : author of the answer – filter to user 1908967  
`posts_answers.creation_date` : creation time – filter to answers **before 2018‑06‑07**  

`votes.post_id` : id of the post (answer) that received the vote – joins to `posts_answers.id`  
`votes.vote_type_id` : kind of vote – 1 = “accept”, 2 = “up‑vote”; only these two are used  
`votes.creation_date` : (not strictly needed but could be used for extra date filtering)  

`posts_questions.id` : question id – joins to `posts_answers.parent_id`  
`posts_questions.tags` : string like “`<java><spring>`”; individual tags are extracted from here  

Main conditions

• `posts_answers.owner_user_id = 1908967`  
• `posts_answers.creation_date < '2018‑06‑07'`  
• `votes.vote_type_id IN (1,2)` (only for the qualifying answers)  

Below are ten exploratory–to–final queries (all capped with `LIMIT 20`, except the last one which returns exactly 10 rows) illustrating the steps that lead to the final answer.

```sql
-- 1) Inspect a few answers written by user 1908967
SELECT id, parent_id, creation_date, score
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
WHERE  owner_user_id = 1908967
  AND  creation_date < '2018-06-07'
ORDER  BY creation_date DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Look at votes the above answers have received (any vote type)
SELECT v.post_id, v.vote_type_id, COUNT(*) AS votes
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`  a
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.votes`          v
       ON v.post_id = a.id
WHERE  a.owner_user_id = 1908967
  AND  a.creation_date < '2018-06-07'
GROUP  BY v.post_id, v.vote_type_id
ORDER  BY v.post_id
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Count only up‑votes (vote_type_id = 2) for each answer
SELECT v.post_id, COUNT(*) AS upvotes
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` a
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.votes`         v
       ON v.post_id = a.id
WHERE  a.owner_user_id = 1908967
  AND  a.creation_date < '2018-06-07'
  AND  v.vote_type_id = 2
GROUP  BY v.post_id
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Count only accepted‑answer votes (vote_type_id = 1) for each answer
SELECT v.post_id, COUNT(*) AS accepted_flags
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` a
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.votes`         v
       ON v.post_id = a.id
WHERE  a.owner_user_id = 1908967
  AND  a.creation_date < '2018-06-07'
  AND  v.vote_type_id = 1
GROUP  BY v.post_id
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Combine the two counts and compute the “per‑answer” score
WITH votes AS (
  SELECT v.post_id,
         SUM(CASE WHEN v.vote_type_id = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS up,
         SUM(CASE WHEN v.vote_type_id = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS acc
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` a
  JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.votes`         v
         ON v.post_id = a.id
  WHERE  a.owner_user_id = 1908967
    AND  a.creation_date < '2018-06-07'
    AND  v.vote_type_id IN (1,2)
  GROUP  BY v.post_id
)
SELECT post_id,
       up, acc,
       10*up + 15*acc AS answer_score
FROM   votes
ORDER  BY answer_score DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Attach the question id to every answer together with its score
WITH answer_scores AS (
  SELECT a.id                              AS answer_id,
         a.parent_id                       AS question_id,
         10*SUM(CASE WHEN v.vote_type_id = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) +
         15*SUM(CASE WHEN v.vote_type_id = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS answer_score
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` a
  JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.votes`         v
         ON v.post_id = a.id
  WHERE  a.owner_user_id = 1908967
    AND  a.creation_date < '2018-06-07'
    AND  v.vote_type_id IN (1,2)
  GROUP  BY answer_id, question_id
)
SELECT *
FROM   answer_scores
ORDER  BY answer_score DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Take those questions and show their raw <tag> string
SELECT q.id, q.tags
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` q
JOIN   (
        SELECT DISTINCT parent_id AS question_id
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
        WHERE owner_user_id = 1908967
          AND creation_date < '2018-06-07'
       ) a
       ON q.id = a.question_id
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Split the <tag> string to individual tags (one row per tag)
SELECT q.id AS question_id,
       tag
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` q,
       UNNEST(REGEXP_EXTRACT_ALL(q.tags, r'<([^>]*)>')) AS tag
WHERE  q.id IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT parent_id
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
        WHERE owner_user_id = 1908967
          AND creation_date < '2018-06-07'
      )
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Join answer‑scores with the exploded tags
WITH answer_scores AS (
  SELECT a.id   AS answer_id,
         a.parent_id AS question_id,
         10*SUM(CASE WHEN v.vote_type_id = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) +
         15*SUM(CASE WHEN v.vote_type_id = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS answer_score
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` a
  JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.votes`         v
         ON v.post_id = a.id
  WHERE  a.owner_user_id = 1908967
    AND  a.creation_date < '2018-06-07'
    AND  v.vote_type_id IN (1,2)
  GROUP  BY answer_id, question_id
),
question_tags AS (
  SELECT q.id AS question_id,
         tag
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` q,
         UNNEST(REGEXP_EXTRACT_ALL(q.tags, r'<([^>]*)>')) AS tag
)
SELECT at.tag,
       ascr.answer_score
FROM   answer_scores ascr
JOIN   question_tags  at
       ON at.question_id = ascr.question_id
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL – compute total score per tag and list top‑10
WITH answer_scores AS (
  SELECT a.id   AS answer_id,
         a.parent_id AS question_id,
         10*SUM(CASE WHEN v.vote_type_id = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) +
         15*SUM(CASE WHEN v.vote_type_id = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS answer_score
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` a
  JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.votes`         v
         ON v.post_id = a.id
  WHERE  a.owner_user_id = 1908967
    AND  a.creation_date < '2018-06-07'
    AND  v.vote_type_id IN (1,2)
  GROUP  BY answer_id, question_id
),
question_tags AS (
  SELECT q.id AS question_id,
         tag
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` q,
         UNNEST(REGEXP_EXTRACT_ALL(q.tags, r'<([^>]*)>')) AS tag
)
SELECT  at.tag,
        SUM(ascr.answer_score) AS total_tag_score
FROM    answer_scores  ascr
JOIN    question_tags  at
        ON at.question_id = ascr.question_id
GROUP   BY at.tag
ORDER   BY total_tag_score DESC
LIMIT   10;
```

Each successive query builds on the previous ones, moving from simple inspection to the final aggregation of the requested “10 × up‑votes + 15 × accepts” metric by tag.
